[2026-05-17 17:13:30] RicBit: Declaring that no further static progress is possible — under any phrasing (ceiling, plateau, converged, taper, exhausted, diminishing returns, "as-complete-as-X-permits") — is governed by the exact same evidence bar as "done": every done-criterion in §"Definition of done" must hold for every file, and you must name the specific unreachable mechanism per region. "~31% of the file disassembles as garbage" is never a ceiling — it is the COMPLETION #1 data-as-code symptom and means you have mislabeled something. A coverage gap is a TODO, not a ceiling.
